  "comments": "Two main types are known.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1</span> - high relief.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2</span> - low relief.<br />\r\nIt is easy to distinguish them by the hair of the Queen and distance of the crown from legend.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span> - high relief, script thicker.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span> - low relief, script thinner, on the left side of the drum 6 pits engraved distinctly.<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d55c8d9b8b55.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d55c8d9b8b55.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"188\" height=\"250\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Combinations</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span> 1990-2000.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span> 2006.",
